    sourceUrl: "https://www.trailwatch.hk/plan-share/279435",
    title: "Tai Mei Tuk (Accessible)",
    titleZh: "大美督（無障礙）",
    desc: "Tai Mei Tuk lies on the eastern edge of Tai Po, backed by Pat Sin Leng and adjacent to Plover Cove Reservoir. The reservoir's main dam, stretching approximately 2.1 kilometres, connects Tai Mei Tuk with Pak Sha Tau. This broad, level path serves not only as an excellent cycling route but also as an accessible hiking trail. Trail Conditions: - Concrete pavement, bicycle lane, road Public Transportation: Kowloon Bus No. 75K and 275R (Service available on Sundays and public holidays) (Get off at Tai Mei Tuk bus terminus) Accessible Toilet: Tai Mei Tuk BBQ Site 1 and 2 Supply Locations: Beverage vending machine at the bus terminus, water refilling station at BBQ Site 1 Recommendations: - Best to go accompanied - Bring enough water and snacks - Check wheelchair equipment (e.g. conditions of wheel, battery) beforehand User comments: The route is 90% flat, making it easily accessible for wheelchair users; two bus services reach the starting point, access is convenient.",
    descZh: "大美督位處大埔東陲，背靠八仙嶺，毗鄰船灣淡水湖。長約2.1公里的淡水湖主堤壩將大美督與白沙頭連接，寬敞平坦的通道不單成為踏單車的好去處，同時也適用作無障礙郊遊路線。 - 水泥行人道、單車徑、馬路 公共交通： 九巴 75K、九巴275R（星期日及公眾假期服務）（大美督總站下車） 無障礙洗手間：大美督一號及二號燒烤場 補給位置：大美督巴士總站的自動飲品販售機、一號燒烤場的加水站 建議事項： - 建議結伴同行 - 要有足夠體力及糧水 - 出發前要先檢查輪椅裝備，如輪軚狀況或電動輪椅的電量等 使用者簡評：路線有9成平路，方便輪椅人士行走；有兩部巴士到達起步點，交通方便。",
    itinerary: "Tai Mei Tuk Bus Terminus › Plover Cove Reservoir Main Dam (Turn back along the same route)",
    itineraryZh: "大美督巴士總站 › 船灣淡水湖主壩（治路折返）",
