    sourceUrl: "https://www.trailwatch.hk/plan-share/278107",
    title: "Shau Kei Wan (Accessible Trail)",
    titleZh: "筲箕灣（無障礙路線）",
    desc: "This route follows the northern coastline of Hong Kong Island's eastern shore, from Quarry Bay to Shau Kei Wan. It passes by the Fireboat Grantham Exhibition Gallery and the Hong Kong Museum of the War of Resistance and Coastal Defence, where visitors can learn about the history of Hong Kong’s sea rescue services through the decommissioned fireboat and the changes in Hong Kong's coastal defence and military affairs through precious exhibits and heritage sites. Distance: Approximately 3.2 km Trail Conditions: Mostly pedestrian paths paved with concrete or stone slab Public transport: [Starting Point] MTR Tai Koo Station (Exit D1) [Finishing Point] MTR Shau Kei Wan Station (Exit B1) Toilets (equipped with barrier-free facilities): Quarry Bay Park Sai Wan Ho Playground Aldrich Bay Promenade Hong Kong Museum of the War of Resistance and Coastal Defence (G/F and 8/F) Locations for Water Filling Station: Sai Wan Ho Playground Aldrich Bay Promenade Hong Kong Museum of the War of Resistance and Coastal Defence (G/F) Recommendations: - Hiking buddies are recommended (MTR train can accommodate multiple wheelchair users) - Ensure you are physically fit for the visit and bring adequate food and water - Check your wheelchair conditions before setting off, such as the condition of wheels and battery level of the electric wheelchair User comments: Some pavements feature uneven surfaces due to exposed tree roots, requiring wheelchair users to proceed slowly to maintain balance. The lower deck passageway of the Fireboat is relatively narrow; wheelchair users are advised to proceed slowly. The upper deck lacks connecting access, preventing wheelchair access. Within the Museum of the War of Resistance and Coastal Defence, both accessible toilets are compact in size. While medium to large wheelchairs may enter with difficulty, they cannot turn around or be used effectively.",
    descZh: "此路線沿著港島東部北岸、由鰂魚涌走到筲箕灣，先後經過葛量洪號滅火輪展覽館和香港抗戰及海防博物館，訪客可從退役的滅火輪了解本地海上救援歷史，並透過珍貴的展品和古蹟探視香港的海防和軍事變遷。 - 磚砌或水泥行人道 公共交通： [起點]：港鐵太古站（D1出口） [終點]：港鐵筲箕灣站（B1出口） 無障礙洗手間：鰂魚涌公園、西灣河遊樂場、愛秩序灣海濱花園、香港抗戰及海防博物館地下及8樓展覽館外 補給位置：西灣河遊樂場、愛秩序灣海濱花園、香港抗戰及海防博物館地下的加水站 建議事項： - 建議結伴同行 - 要有足夠體力及糧水 - 出發前要先檢查輪椅裝備，如輪軚狀況或電動輪椅的展覽館外量等 使用者簡評：部份行人路因樹根外露令路面凹凸不平，輪椅需慢駛免失平衡；滅火輪下層船艙通道較窄，建議輪椅人士慢駛，上層則未有通道接駁，輪椅使用者未能進入；香港抗戰及海防博物館內兩個無障礙洗手間的面積較小，中至大型輪椅能勉強內進但不能掉頭及使用。",
    itinerary: "MTR Tai Koo Station › Quarry Bay Park › Fireboat Alexander Grantham Exhibition Gallery › Tam Kung Temple › Hong Kong Museum of the War of Resistance and Coastal Defence › MTR Shau Kei Wan Station",
